{
    # ============================================================================
    # neuro-san agent network: "lab_ops"
    #
    # A neuro-san coordinator that fronts the mimOE AAOSA mesh. It exposes ALL
    # THREE mimOE agents as EXTERNAL agents (referenced by URL in its tools list)
    # so it can either hand a whole inquiry to the mesh (front_man) or reach a
    # single specialist directly (network_agent / pi_device_agent).
    #
    # The URLs point at neuro-san/adapter.js, which serves the neuro-san external
    # surface (/api/v1/<name>/function + /streaming_chat) and translates each call
    # into the mesh's /chat or /aaosa. Change 127.0.0.1:4747 to wherever you run
    # the adapter.
    # ============================================================================

    # Default LLM for the coordinator's OWN routing + synthesis reasoning. Point
    # this at whatever your neuro-san install is configured to use. To run the
    # coordinator on your local milm instead, register a custom llm in neuro-san's
    # llm_info config and reference it here by name.
    "llm_config": {
        "model_name": "gpt-4o"
    },

    "tools": [

        # ---- Front-man of THIS neuro-san network (the top-level agent) ---------
        {
            "name": "lab_coordinator",
            "function": {
                "description": "Coordinates hardware-lab inquiries by delegating to the mimOE AAOSA mesh and its specialists."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the coordinator for a hardware lab. You have three downstream agents,
all running as EXTERNAL mimOE AAOSA agents:

- front_man: the lab MESH coordinator. Delegating to it runs the whole mesh
  (network + device specialists) and returns one synthesized answer. Prefer it
  for compound or ambiguous questions, or anything that may span specialties.
- network_agent: NETWORK specialist (topology, LAN/WiFi, firewalls, adding
  devices to the mesh, connectivity troubleshooting). Call it directly for a
  pure network question.
- pi_device_agent: Raspberry Pi HEALTH specialist (CPU temperature, load,
  memory, uptime). Call it directly for a question about the device's current
  state or capacity.

Decide which downstream agent(s) can address the user's inquiry and delegate.
For a single-domain question, call the matching specialist directly. For a
multi-part or unclear question, delegate to front_man and let the mesh route it.
Pass the user's inquiry verbatim as the `inquiry` argument, then synthesize the
returned answer(s) into one reply for the user.
""",
            "command": "Determine which downstream agent(s) can address the inquiry, delegate to them, and return a synthesized answer.",

            # External agents, referenced by URL. neuro-san reads each one's
            # /api/v1/<name>/function to learn its signature, then calls
            # /api/v1/<name>/streaming_chat to run it.
            "tools": [
                "http://127.0.0.1:4747/front_man",
                "http://127.0.0.1:4747/network_agent",
                "http://127.0.0.1:4747/pi_device_agent"
            ]
        }
    ]
}
